Ripley and I waterproofed the bus this afternoon. Notes from the day.

<!-- TODO(jess): photo — drop into static/photos/log/waterproofing-seats-and-a-wants-list.<ext>, then an image reference with a one-line credit -->

Waterproofing:

- Worked the body and openings: fiberglass, caulk, measurements for parts
  that need printing.
- Bring sheet metal or plastic if you have it.
- Interim lock solution by end of week.
- Working bus days for now: Thursdays and Fridays, roughly 3 to 5pm.

Seats:

- Pulled three more seats, freed the rear passenger-side bench fasteners.
  Don't sit on it yet.

Wants list:

- A 9/16 impact or breaker bar for one stubborn bolt, cleaning supplies,
  imperial square bits to 7/8 inch, security-torx bits, and help
  spreading the word.

Workshop and meeting:

- Want help workshopping onboarding, checkout, repair, and check-in user
  stories. Basement or a nearby spot next week works.
- Proposed a sit-down next Thursday the 20th at 4pm at the teahouse, on
  asset agreement and liability structure.
